{
  "scenario_id": "hospital-life-safety-isolation-mixed-medgas",
  "title": "Life-safety isolation violation: med-gas on the general panel",
  "description": "The hospital's duplex med-gas manifolds are wired from the general distribution panel instead of the life-safety branch. A general-panel fault exposes the imaging service but is absorbed for med-gas by the manifold N+1 group \u2014 yet the wiring itself violates life-safety isolation, and the assessor must raise the life_safety_isolation finding on the medical-gas service with the violation path as evidence.",
